                <pb facs="0645" n="1605" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1605"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 112.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Said Pasha.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 6,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: On the 17th ultimo, in my note No.
                    34, I had the honor to address you and ask for the production of the evidence
                    against H. A. Proios.</p>
                <p>Mr. Pringle, the consul-general, informs me that it is now eight months since
                    Proios was arrested and imprisoned, and that according to our laws he can not
                    continue to retain him, and that in one week from to day he will consider
                    himself bound to release him unless evidence be brought against him. I therefore
                    respectfully ask for your immediate attention to the matter.</p>
                <p>Accept, excellency, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton King</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
